sbe1v1k: dts: start lan1 (QCA8081) in 2500base-x  [test item]

QCA8081 has no USXGMII. Its SerDes runs SGMII at 10/100/1000 and
2500BASE-X at 2.5G, and qca808x_read_status() reports which one is in
use, so phylink already switches the PCS to SGMII or 2500BASE-X at
link-up. "usxgmii" only selected the initial (pre-link) mode, which made
the PCS run the USXGMII/XPCS bring-up for a PHY that never speaks it.
Use 2500base-x like the 8devices Kiwi (also QCA8081 on uniphy1).
"managed = in-band-status" stays: SGMII uses in-band AN; for 2500BASE-X
the PCS reports LINK_INBAND_DISABLE only, so phylink falls back to
outband/PHY mode on its own.

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9570-sbe1v1k.dts b/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9570-sbe1v1k.dts
--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9570-sbe1v1k.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9570-sbe1v1k.dts
@@ -449,7 +449,13 @@
 
 		port@5 {
 			reg = <5>;
-			phy-mode = "usxgmii";
+			/*
+			 * QCA8081 has no USXGMII: its SerDes runs SGMII up to
+			 * 1G and 2500BASE-X at 2.5G, and the PHY driver reports
+			 * which one is in use. Start in 2500BASE-X like other
+			 * IPQ9574 boards with this PHY (8devices Kiwi).
+			 */
+			phy-mode = "2500base-x";
 			phy-handle = <&qca8081_28>;
 			pcs-handle = <&pcs1_ch0>;
 			managed = "in-band-status";
